                  sagging. A few more age spots. Skin that just looks… tired.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Zu1G2h3gBROz"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ft4O1rxcnLGf"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-AiDWkSlRU5OG"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-w78OaKj2WsxT"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ft4O1rxcnLGf"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-DvNMulAImXlY">You smiled. You hugged her. You told her she looked
                  amazing.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-AUNid3KVOLxO"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ft4O1rxcnLGf"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-JeAjI2UzIBDN"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2zmkF2r4u4Cj"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ft4O1rxcnLGf"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-RIsUMMFiUyN1">And then you drove home asking yourself the same question
                  every woman over 50 asks at some point:</span></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-joMsVFJyx28N" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-t9vfBzSJy2jF"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vGTPtPp7n0ov"><i id="cc-id-l99u5VSwK9mB" class="rte-styled-text">"What is SHE doing that I'm not?"</i><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-jKCBAeJqh9t1"></span></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-2g8RGQndAmUq" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ESOW9CmULkl1">It's tempting to chalk it up to lucky genes.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-p4oZT0gH2plz"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-NgxZ1CTaHiPI"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-EKyV8PS7Dp5W"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-U4gVuaIIC0jG">Or some $3,000 laser treatment her husband paid for.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-HYkrnM1ZMUOn"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-XnBUgKlYkopQ"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ChJhyDJWDy6S"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-rBlwKbdV4Ehw">Or a Beverly Hills dermatologist she has on speed dial.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-q9yx0zkNqHnD"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-xa4TsfagfcYz"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-8xMGrI0luLa4"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-67pTt0uEAXvx">But the answer is none of those things.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ku4kJROfCZI9"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-3Ra6GP9lQDbx"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-dcSjzMVqyo2O"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-TexFRTlAXaXL"><b id="cc-id-ouvL1DfJCuCA" class="rte-styled-text">And for the last 14 years, one woman has been quietly
                    putting the pieces together…</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-kj7plN5UnPrF"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-E6Rm5kqj9VRF"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7">
                Her name is Sabine Wolff.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-rbyXl6qW0ig3"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-NUoz1JpKn2eS"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7">
                She's a licensed aesthetician at a high-end skin clinic in
                Scottsdale, Arizona.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-fNAKmjDfD1Hu"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-85hifHNt8RVx"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7">
                And she's looked at more faces up close than almost anyone alive
                — over
                <b id="cc-id-gVaNbDbLTDm0" class="rte-styled-text">6,000 of them.</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-FAkj4VcML8IZ"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-grIdgqShHjJP"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7">
                Peels. Extractions. Microneedling. LED therapy. You name it,
                she's done it.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-st23doaCqdtj"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-5OX3pvZpGLkC"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7">
                But here's what makes Sabine different from every other
                aesthetician you've ever met…<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-okxdMnB7tSeg"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-JfdVrhzcmVQj"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7">
                It's not what she does during the treatment.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vMNNogiAzFw0"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-5P211WqLAJhe"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vltwMJlZ0NN7">
                It's what she sees
                <b id="cc-id-Nqxh1lgMYf6O" class="rte-styled-text">before it even begins.</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ywCTPy4wa0t2"></div></div><img class="fk-image-defaults fk-disable-lazy" src="{{ '1777303033485_image.webp' | asset_url }}" id="cc-id-3gZZ89ARxXVo" title="" href="" onclick="" target="_self" alt="" align="center" width="" height=""><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-F139kJrF6TtQ" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                "The second a woman sits in my chair and I turn on the
                magnifying lamp, I can read her skin like a book," Sabine
                says.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-r285np1McoV2"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-BPt6DGZSnGq6"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                "I can tell how old her skin really is. I can see what's coming
                in the next 5 years. And most of the time… I can see exactly why
                she's losing the battle."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-0waLL1fpio60"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-xxNkPtXqKbtz"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                Because in 14 years — and 6,000 faces — Sabine says she's
                noticed a pattern almost no one in the beauty industry is
                willing to talk about.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-9fBpiedlHR2O"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-686eLiChRSUp"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                Out of every 50 women over 50 who walk through her door…<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WAi25dEYifW0"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-gaezHDzhw5h8"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-AEYTvgKin49Q"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><b id="cc-id-IHn2PS6Ukur7" class="rte-styled-text">49 of them</b>
                look the same under that lamp.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-meE2N1d1KQ4p"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-kQoaWNvEFQMa"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                The surface is "treated." Moisturized. Covered in serums.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-sgRau7SRUBPu"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qhSbgELgnLVY"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                But underneath? Something else is quietly falling apart.
                Something no cream on her counter is touching.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-yCYMYKu0fWik"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-PTyyEVx5prDj"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                And then there's the<b id="cc-id-WwASYrQePVgr" class="rte-styled-text">
                  1 in 50…</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Vx12zMRCgtyv"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br id="cc-id-6sfbN6zWzFAA"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                The woman whose skin is firm in a way you just can't fake.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-XQO8gr4rkQQW"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-rktt8sbOXlpX"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                Not tight from a cream. Not plumped up for a few hours by a
                serum.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-5TvOWsG9MuEI"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-sUf0qTN5Akli"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                Actually firm. From the inside out.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-yWwZIR0NxxBd"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-PUs4Y87XngiV"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WQzWR8KVIaFk">
                "The moment I see that kind of skin under the lamp," Sabine
                says, "I know she's doing something 99% of women have never even
                heard of."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-JxO4qpSDfyId"></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-5Cpp8lQ8nwpr">
              “After 6,000 Facials, One Name Kept Showing Up In My Notebook”<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-GdNEcpqRlTpy"></div><img class="fk-image-defaults fk-disable-lazy" src="{{ '1766001028480_0f26ef1a_4414_405e_8041_c92303d9a8e3.webp' | asset_url }}" id="cc-id-Q7DvGLdSsj2o" title="" href="" onclick="" target="_self" alt="" align="center" width="" height=""><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-tNn3BLfzRuS3" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16">
                Four years ago, Sabine started keeping track.<br id="cc-id-fPBtefLftaJH" class="rte-styled-text" data-layer-name="Br"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-hVg1VR9daLqB"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16">
                Not officially. Not for a study.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Iel8t8rRs4Rr"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J5DxI8My5pJa"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16">
                Just a notebook she kept in her desk drawer.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPPPqbUvBw7x"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-hxwFiqWZCdFk"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16">
                Every time a woman over 50 sat in her chair with skin that
                didn't match her age… Sabine wrote her name down.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-kj4XZSDZLYRZ"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vWudvsGhJPjF"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16">
                After four years, she had
                <b id="cc-id-e4pJijlyZ67P" class="rte-styled-text">47 names.</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-kIIXZZ5BPO7i"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16"><br id="cc-id-3fbcK4mRtprN"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16">
                47 women out of roughly 2,400 clients over 50.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-OjvxiZg0DTGU"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-wVX7K2HQSd1C"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16">
                Less than 2%.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-QhTKTEM47HXf"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-j83W9QlGBm6U"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-J7kamdraka16">
                "Those 47 women became my obsession," Sabine says.
              </div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-f9zOuV7Ogy2E" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-HNORZHfZsKnp"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-IIVlrO4l9N4x"><i id="cc-id-Hmh1UuDFqkxA" class="rte-styled-text">"Because their skin wasn't just 'good for their age.' It
                    was healthier than women fifteen years younger. My
                    elasticity readings proved it. My hydration tests proved it.
                    Everything I could measure told me the same thing —
                    something was different about these women. Something that
                    was working deeper than any cream I'd ever seen."</i><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-F7KFHFCW88qB"></span></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-qIaMN47efnwC" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-4vYuykYst085">
                So Sabine did something she'd never done in her career.<br id="cc-id-tjwHzYzNXoBa"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-4vYuykYst085"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-hNXuWy896kcf"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-4vYuykYst085">
                She started asking questions.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-BZYpPQJz1SMb"></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-BSt0yBsGY32I" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-MnlYl9auuhJE"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UH6R3j01GdOW"><i id="cc-id-j4l7uuXl29ak" class="rte-styled-text">"What are you doing that's different?"</i><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-h8D0l5MVhMnT"></span></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-Ls53LFu92mZV" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-0OTt6ziR88Pu">
                Over the next six months, she tracked down every single one of
                the 47.<br id="cc-id-76TW0HZ4AAvn"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-0OTt6ziR88Pu"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vwKJHUzRGTe5"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-0OTt6ziR88Pu">
                Some she caught during appointments. Others she met for coffee
                at the Prickly Pear cafe down the street from her clinic. A few
                she called on the phone.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-BZYTuJNMlQ9T"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-0OTt6ziR88Pu"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-HKmwJi6lo0bx"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-0OTt6ziR88Pu">
                And she asked every one of them the same question:<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ywlHjOTJ8PPE"></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-RfjQhiz8Y4w3" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-408PrJcxJqIL"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-86JNng0XjntO"><i id="cc-id-nNT3iQxaAOmy" class="rte-styled-text">"Walk me through exactly what you put on your skin. Morning
                    and night. Every step."</i><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-e3iRJmooaQYm"></span></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-oGBBTR2iwTaT" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp" style="text-align: left !important;"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD">
                The answers floored her.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-MfwWA3KZ2p3u"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-kVrL96ftMWWw"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD">
                "I expected to hear about prescription creams. Expensive serums.
                Some secret high-end brand from France or Korea. That's what
                most of my clients use — women spending $300 to $600 a month on
                7-step routines."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ZOOZopiNgAM2"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-DU3vY77ugVFy"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD">
                "Instead… I heard the complete opposite."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-V3MZebuobk7D"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-iirduE6L418c"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD">
                Of the 47 women Sabine spoke to:<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-i0BAWFrdDFnu"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-enWz1odEyLFg"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD"><ul class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-KwePT3bHCuaN"><li class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ZWPr2lfuxsym"><b id="cc-id-SjYsKZ7E7PiU" class="rte-styled-text">41</b>
                    used three products or fewer each day
                  </li><li class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Kyi3nptRDZrO"><b id="cc-id-5cMo8koJuD2a" class="rte-styled-text">33</b>
                    used just one serum as their main anti-aging step
                  </li><li class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-mwwSJLcbOMRy"><b id="cc-id-8ajzl6evae32" class="rte-styled-text">28</b>
                    had actually simplified their routine in the last two years
                    — meaning they used to use MORE and switched to LESS
                  </li><li class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-rUUD0IqjlBwE">
                    And
                    <b id="cc-id-X0YaZQB530Hd" class="rte-styled-text">19 of them — </b>nineteen out of forty-seven — were using the exact same
                    product
                  </li></ul></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD">
                "When the same name kept coming up — over and over — from women
                who didn't know each other, who lived in different parts of
                Phoenix, with different skin types and different lives…"<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-H2pziPFozCOP"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-8UOJZro0N4aD"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD">
                "I knew I'd found something."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-4hUT1snJzyPN"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-F1arRSCeD0cU"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2vx1H0DwyzwD">
                The product was called
                <b id="cc-id-gkEjczoN1VFl" class="rte-styled-text">Olavita</b>.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-LBkIrBOJyV3G"></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-HPOmh6qh3Stz">
              For the last 30 years, women have been told the same story:<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-tUvNZmbHVAug"></div><img class="fk-image-defaults fk-disable-lazy" src="{{ '1777398719302_s04_collagen_myth.webp' | asset_url }}" id="cc-id-2VNdIlOl3hMm" title="" href="" onclick="" target="_self" alt="" align="center" width="" height=""><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-0Cm0QFpWCLql" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ZMygaWMK12yP"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-PK60ErrYhp2B">"Your skin ages because you're losing collagen. So put more
                  collagen back in."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qo8KKc0kgmVy"></span></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-QsrXLdbjnMwg" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                Every cream. Every serum. Every commercial on daytime TV.<br id="cc-id-wT6SCsTnpX21" class="rte-styled-text" data-layer-name="Br"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-V2X8fvfzZgkL"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                All chasing the same thing.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-PIG2Q2qkvtfD"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-jVgcNWgF4Pgc"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                And all missing the real problem by a mile.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-BCzgVDVIDV9J"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-jQ29GvqsoCEr"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                "Collagen loss is a
                <b id="cc-id-g2q52QtOQiKe" class="rte-styled-text">symptom</b>,"
                Sabine says. "Not the cause. Chasing it is like mopping the
                floor while the pipe is still leaking."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-kKf8w0S3UDwu"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-zQspq30lR1D1"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                So what IS the real cause?<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-URhYtYc2fEnl"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-p9od8nw4aviK"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                Two words most women have never heard in their lives:<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-1PE04FZwBVqz"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2cO8v1uwSvqJ"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><b id="cc-id-iAKoITfElTgA" class="rte-styled-text">Fibroblast Failure.</b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Zy9ArUGh6olf"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                Here's what they are, in plain English.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Ns3lCi1ibHVY"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-IN3ZootSE9Zn"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                Fibroblasts are tiny cells that live deep beneath your skin — in
                a layer no cream ever reaches.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-cPZDwIWpPPRi"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Vv4LahakwB7y"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                Think of them as the construction crew that holds your face
                together.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-iHeJvr1urcT0"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-u4xIkzhiPRey"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                Their job is to build collagen. Build elastin. Keep your skin
                firm and lifted from the INSIDE.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vscq4fOaUoWt"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-lUQchDzk21Dn"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                When they're young and active, your skin looks young too. Plump.
                Bouncy. Taut.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-05qDG44YRnbB"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-DIZ9GH584G3F"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                But somewhere in your 40s… these cells start slowing down.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-BShgNW9iY5UF"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-xg6nq2HgTCk7"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                By your 50s, most of them go dormant. Asleep on the job.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ATAWaxDIhgBP"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-7W1XZ0xvf0RY"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                The scaffolding weakens. Skin sags. Wrinkles deepen. Crepey
                texture shows up seemingly overnight.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Mw7ZQNxSwBhl"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-8KitsF7PG35F"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                And no "collagen-boosting" cream you smear on top can do a thing
                about it.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-BMyx3UXUWy59"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-6AKGqpcSgLPX"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                Because those products never reach the fibroblasts. They sit on
                the surface, do a little hydrating, and wash off in the
                shower.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-8r89ycAXSNdH"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-L3vk8A3ZgG93"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                "That's why 99% of skincare fails women over 50," Sabine says.
                "They're painting the walls while the foundation is cracking
                underneath."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-gMN0N0EYfIWc"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-GAuKMeh5U4B5"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><b id="cc-id-FZgs3qsEaLeI" class="rte-styled-text">This is where Olavita is different.</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-6zYyt401MY25"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-41fzBy7c38AK"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                It doesn't chase collagen. It doesn't just hydrate the top
                layer.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-H20k1CQZJIkW"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ZsrN8Gz5p4xG"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                It goes straight for the fibroblasts — waking them up and
                putting the construction crew back to work.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-iLdo7jdZ0ZrM"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-PNnuhAS5ibJV"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                And when those cells come back online… they do exactly what they
                did in your 30s.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Vxj2CdYGiLNZ"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-t9dzpB5A9Ysr"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                They build collagen. They build elastin. They rebuild your
                skin's support system from underneath.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-7nXePTyYpDkY"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ytFXSR1dt2x0"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                That's why those 19 women in Sabine's notebook looked the way
                they did.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Dgg9s1tB9K9N"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-10sunccJdd1X"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                It wasn't because they were using more products.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-gQU1guwrnLj6"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ucSxWnsj94QT"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qHEA5XRlRWhE">
                It's because they were using the
                <b id="cc-id-uIyrvDA1SjQC" class="rte-styled-text">one</b>
                product that actually worked at the level where real aging
                happens.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Q9d9SwA53O9m"></div></div><img class="fk-image-defaults fk-disable-lazy" src="{{ '1777394519893_jessica_s07_v4a.webp' | asset_url }}" id="cc-id-yo4B8mRjO2XK" title="" href="" onclick="" target="_self" alt="" align="center" width="" height=""><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-I5EbBtMBKFOK" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b id="cc-id-Y5HMIzEkEzRe" class="rte-styled-text">Six pharmaceutical-grade compounds. Each one engineered to do
                  something most skincare simply can't do — reach the dermis and
                  wake up dormant fibroblasts.</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-StrMC1UHg1da"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-CTAD1GM0JSOq"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-EL8zQcl1KMrY"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b id="cc-id-QJ102ZX62DDZ" class="rte-styled-text">1. Matrixyl Synthe'6 —</b>
                a patented peptide that signals six different structural
                components of your skin to start rebuilding at once. In clinical
                studies, it reduced wrinkle depth by an average of
                <b id="cc-id-ajaYtogEW0sa" class="rte-styled-text">31% in 60 days.</b>
                Not by "filling in" wrinkles from the outside. By waking up the
                cells underneath them to rebuild from within.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ZUJgVD9OdT1F"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-PLrmB2Btoeap"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vzJYRL3OqhRw"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b id="cc-id-21dEx2nurjkG" class="rte-styled-text">2. Matrixyl-3000 —</b>
                goes directly to dormant fibroblasts and flips them back on.
                Clinical data shows collagen production jumps by up to<b id="cc-id-emuwZRhyWA4m" class="rte-styled-text">
                  350%.</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-8dXu8aJX3w8a"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-uVCZCObOwtzt"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz">
                That number isn't a typo.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-GaDhlEwTTSwI"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-HMGMz5qYhJBQ"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Tyzd4loYTk4x"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b id="cc-id-pON6Iw2bosst" class="rte-styled-text">3. Argireline —</b>
                known in dermatology circles as "topical Botox." Relaxes the
                tiny muscles that cause expression lines — forehead creases,
                crow's feet, the "11"s between your brows. No needles. No frozen
                face.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-aRtrE58YCUy2"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-mGtINbNKKuHn"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-uK5xOa97hCyy"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b id="cc-id-wBRTtUHL7fHB" class="rte-styled-text">4. Stay-C 50 —</b>
                a stabilized form of Vitamin C that doesn't oxidize on your skin
                or stain your pillowcase the way regular Vitamin C serums do.
                Targets dark spots, sun damage, and uneven tone at the cellular
                level.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-bv3jW7bsonJz"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-g9chFRkWnLrO"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-g8NmIS7m9vcW"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b id="cc-id-iJIhDeMImlrM" class="rte-styled-text">5. Bioactive Collagen Peptides —</b>
                collagen fragments small enough to actually penetrate past the
                surface. These aren't the oversized molecules in your $120 cream
                that just sit on top of your skin. These are sized to reach the
                dermis — where they can actually be used.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-IsrJIHB3nvvr"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-HsTTirBNsnXb"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-w7YjoIUipPH9"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WPwcUgv9cTkz"><b id="cc-id-dEJ7djn93XCP" class="rte-styled-text">6. Ceramide Complex —</b>
                rebuilds your skin's protective barrier and locks in hydration
                for 24+ hours. Without it, everything else you put on your face
                just evaporates.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-p4kyzjrdNODK"></div></div><img class="fk-image-defaults fk-disable-lazy" src="{{ '1777029282042_5.webp' | asset_url }}" id="cc-id-od7LoHrec2JH" title="" href="" onclick="" target="_self" alt="" align="center" width="" height=""><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-DfzPCdiMn2Vt" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx">
                "When I looked at this formula for the first time, it clicked,"
                Sabine says.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-8E7dclzo5wZI"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-zH3h28gPYNRX"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx">
                "I finally understood why those 19 women had the skin they
                had."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-GS0wafC4n8pM"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-5SzFxiCNhZA5"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx">
                "This wasn't a moisturizer pretending to be anti-aging. This was
                actual dermal-level intervention — in a bottle."<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-p9BhGcHq0T3d"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-m0ZFjCfZbkEU"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx">
                And the best part?<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-RMiZ2taDaPOb"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-eOqIKa4XtJbW"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx">
                The whole routine takes
                <b id="cc-id-LrTkLbTpmlIZ" class="rte-styled-text">seven seconds.</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ameT6j7Ozrvy"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-uWlWeOE3tvde"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-P6nBwNiKFrqq"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-OUi0uUZMokPI">Three drops. Massaged into face and neck. Once every
                  morning.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-wkRU937cgLrH"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ZOtA889GyQ87"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-RyfGpIVb0UmK"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-VJL1eR5wmq7n">That's it.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-SeUCzXemvsia"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-o7WKjhAUw2ds"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-zRhvbTgDZBJi"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-mEfA1LG1s5sk">No 10-step routine. No layering. No toners or essences or
                  weekly masks.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-gAZXCYMVoNUy"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-sTpwFMdNygGH"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-uPni6khtQWIe"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFLFpytQ0GRx"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Bb4d36lo7b9t">Three drops. Seven seconds. Done.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-sxYnk5Yz7ZHW"></span></div></div><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-q4tlnAf5FzgM">
              Women Are Seeing Amazing Results<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-5NF7jF1eWrqy"></div><img class="fk-image-defaults fk-disable-lazy" src="{{ '1777029301236_6.webp' | asset_url }}" id="cc-id-FB1gaZwVaDTQ" title="" href="" onclick="" target="_self" alt="" align="center" width="" height=""><div data-text="text" id="cc-id-OEg40HvB7xXT" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776990628614_img1_second.webp"><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-QDEZRSSJKSkI"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-M4Aes9GJC0eL"><b id="cc-id-4Fnq8vqrHqJO" class="rte-styled-text">Monica, 59 — Paradise Valley, AZ</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Qp3fPJNIFd4K"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-QDEZRSSJKSkI">
                "Sabine measured my skin in January and again in March. My
